    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.25036_p9_b14",
      "text": "Impact Statement\n",
      "bbox": [
        307.44,
        475.48,
        398.74,
        487.43
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        1229,
        1901,
        1594,
        1949
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 11.96,
      "font_name": "NimbusRomNo9L-Medi",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 16,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.25036_p9_b15",
      "text": "This paper presents work whose goal is to advance the field\nof Machine Learning, specifically focusing on improving the\nreliability and visual faithfulness of Large Vision-Language\nModels (LVLMs). By mitigating language bias and reduc-\ning hallucinations, our proposed methods (LBR and LBP)\ncontribute to the development of safer and more trustwor-\nthy AI systems. This is particularly critical for real-world\napplications where model factuality is paramount. We do\nnot foresee any immediate negative societal consequences\nspecific to this work, beyond the general risks associated\nwith the advancement of generative AI models.\n",
      "bbox": [
        307.08,
        496.52,
        543.09,
        625.99
      ],
